(2286180, 313784, 52790, '<td valign="top">the halo around these flowers hurts my eyes, you have gone overboard with the editing, and the actual flowers have very little contrast. next time pic your background a little better so that you aren''t forced to do a bit of cloning/painting/burning to get the desired image. adjust your levels (if you have photoshop) or contrast with any other software, to get more detail in the image.</td>', 'the halo around these flowers hurts my eyes, you have gone overboard with the editing, and the actual flowers have very little contrast. next time pic your background a little better so that you aren''t forced to do a bit of cloning/painting/burning to get the desired image. adjust your levels (if you have photoshop) or contrast with any other software, to get more detail in the image.', '2006-04-04 12:24:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286182, 313842, 52790, '<td valign="top">finally an image with vibraint colors, good detail, and great contrast</td>', 'finally an image with vibraint colors, good detail, and great contrast', '2006-04-04 12:25:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286194, 313888, 43463, '<td valign="top">Love the colors and presentation of the flowers in this shot! The flowers are in lovely bloom and sharp focus. Beautifully done and captured. This is a really good shot but it could be even better. As it stands now the areas of brightness and vibrancy rests more in the sky than in the properties of the flowers. Because they are in the foreground and are stereotypically brilliant and bold in hue they should be the ones that are dominating the scene with their vibrant colors. Instead their tones are more subdued and darker. My suggestion is to (if you can) manaully adjusted the settings to underexposure, and use the flash to get the right exposure on the flowers. This will give you a "studio" feel on a cloudy bright day. As an example this photographer managed to capture this //www.deviantart.com/view/30533681/   and I think you could do the same with this composition.</td>', 'Love the colors and presentation of the flowers in this shot! The flowers are in lovely bloom and sharp focus. Beautifully done and captured. This is a really good shot but it could be even better. As it stands now the areas of brightness and vibrancy rests more in the sky than in the properties of the flowers. Because they are in the foreground and are stereotypically brilliant and bold in hue they should be the ones that are dominating the scene with their vibrant colors. Instead their tones are more subdued and darker. My suggestion is to (if you can) manaully adjusted the settings to underexposure, and use the flash to get the right exposure on the flowers. This will give you a "studio" feel on a cloudy bright day. As an example this photographer managed to capture this //www.deviantart.com/view/30533681/   and I think you could do the same with this composition.', '2006-04-04 12:28:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286198, 315734, 52790, '<td valign="top">i really like this image, but i see some room for improvement.<br/>-boost he green and yellow saturation levels to get more vibrant colors<br/>-use a faster shutter speed to truely freeze the action, as is the water is a bit blurry<br/>-reduce the amount of light hitting your background, or move your background further away so that you aren''t getting so much light bouncing back<br/>-slightly tweak your levels, to get just a little more detail and contrast.</td>', 'i really like this image, but i see some room for improvement.-boost he green and yellow saturation levels to get more vibrant colors-use a faster shutter speed to truely freeze the action, as is the water is a bit blurry-reduce the amount of light hitting your background, or move your background further away so that you aren''t getting so much light bouncing back-slightly tweak your levels, to get just a little more detail and contrast.', '2006-04-04 12:29:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286210, 314327, 52790, '<td valign="top">i don''t know what editing software you are using, but i would suggest if you are using photoshop to go into the hue/saturation adjustments, select "yellow" from the drop down menu and then slide the saturation up a bit, i think it would have helped this image tremendously, i like it as is, but would give it the extra punch</td>', 'i don''t know what editing software you are using, but i would suggest if you are using photoshop to go into the hue/saturation adjustments, select "yellow" from the drop down menu and then slide the saturation up a bit, i think it would have helped this image tremendously, i like it as is, but would give it the extra punch', '2006-04-04 12:34:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286212, 313963, 52790, '<td valign="top">just a bit too orange, for a yellow, but good image none-the-less</td>', 'just a bit too orange, for a yellow, but good image none-the-less', '2006-04-04 12:35:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286218, 314726, 52790, '<td valign="top">is image is way too low resolution, horrible lighting and complete lack of contrast, if you were to attempt the image in the future, i would suggest doing the following:<br/>find a center of interest, move in on the actualy flower cluster, and focus on one flower<br/>make sure you save it at a high enough resolution that you don''t loose detail and get the jpg, edge noise<br/>pay attention to your lighting, side lighting probably would have worked best<br/>in post-editing, boost your yellow saturation, and then add a bit of contrast</td>', 'is image is way too low resolution, horrible lighting and complete lack of contrast, if you were to attempt the image in the future, i would suggest doing the following:find a center of interest, move in on the actualy flower cluster, and focus on one flowermake sure you save it at a high enough resolution that you don''t loose detail and get the jpg, edge noisepay attention to your lighting, side lighting probably would have worked bestin post-editing, boost your yellow saturation, and then add a bit of contrast', '2006-04-04 12:39:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286223, 315012, 42100, '<td valign="top">Very nice composition.  The darker tones in the stems really gives the photo some mood.  Well done!</td>', 'Very nice composition.  The darker tones in the stems really gives the photo some mood.  Well done!', '2006-04-04 12:41:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286224, 314788, 43463, '<td valign="top">A beautifully composed picture that upon viewing Sting''s song "Fields of Gold" began playing in my head. The yellow hues of the swaying flowers dominate the scene of this composition. Part of me would like to have the flowers in the foreground in sharper focus while another part likes the soft off focus look for it adds motion to the shot. I think and feel the breeze that blows over the swaying flowers. I think the model adds visual interest as she sits and reflects in this golden field. Lastly my only critique on this piece is that I wish that she had positioned her knee to be concealed by the flowers. The reason is because it detracts from the scene in which she is surrounded by this field of flowers. The upraised knee blocks the view of the flowers behind her and breaks up the vision of her being encircled by this sea of golden beauty.</td>', 'A beautifully composed picture that upon viewing Sting''s song "Fields of Gold" began playing in my head. The yellow hues of the swaying flowers dominate the scene of this composition. Part of me would like to have the flowers in the foreground in sharper focus while another part likes the soft off focus look for it adds motion to the shot. I think and feel the breeze that blows over the swaying flowers. I think the model adds visual interest as she sits and reflects in this golden field. Lastly my only critique on this piece is that I wish that she had positioned her knee to be concealed by the flowers. The reason is because it detracts from the scene in which she is surrounded by this field of flowers. The upraised knee blocks the view of the flowers behind her and breaks up the vision of her being encircled by this sea of golden beauty.', '2006-04-04 12:41:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286226, 315313, 43463, '<td valign="top">Bright, cheerful and sunny are the words that I would use to describe this composition. This photo is very much springtime picnic with a cup of tea personified:-) Yellows are bold and vibrant and that splash of pink just adds another cheerful spring color for visual interest. The reflections on the teapot are a tad distracting and a good polorizer lens would eliminate those reflections. While the white background helps make the main subject stand out it creates a stark and sterile feel that is the exact opposite of the cheery, springtime mood you are creating with the flowers &amp; teapot. Perhaps another color that is readily associated with spring would be a better compliment to the main object present in the photo - say a solid mint or grass green background - perhaps even a bright checkerboard pattern that children''s artist Mary Engelbreit is fond of using in her borders would help boast that springtime bright colorful presentation seen in your photo.</td>', 'Bright, cheerful and sunny are the words that I would use to describe this composition. This photo is very much springtime picnic with a cup of tea personified:-) Yellows are bold and vibrant and that splash of pink just adds another cheerful spring color for visual interest. The reflections on the teapot are a tad distracting and a good polorizer lens would eliminate those reflections. While the white background helps make the main subject stand out it creates a stark and sterile feel that is the exact opposite of the cheery, springtime mood you are creating with the flowers & teapot. Perhaps another color that is readily associated with spring would be a better compliment to the main object present in the photo - say a solid mint or grass green background - perhaps even a bright checkerboard pattern that children''s artist Mary Engelbreit is fond of using in her borders would help boast that springtime bright colorful presentation seen in your photo.', '2006-04-04 12:43:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286236, 315228, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hello Angie. I mean Pedro ;) I guess Banana Republic had a half off sale eh? Dude you rock in portrait photography. Lighting, model and setup are all great! My only thought? Raise the sunglasses a but higher on her head. Good luck!</td>', 'Hello Angie. I mean Pedro ;) I guess Banana Republic had a half off sale eh? Dude you rock in portrait photography. Lighting, model and setup are all great! My only thought? Raise the sunglasses a but higher on her head. Good luck!', '2006-04-04 12:46:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286243, 314547, 52790, '<td valign="top">i think i know whos this is, and i love it regardless of the photographer. i hope it does well</td>', 'i think i know whos this is, and i love it regardless of the photographer. i hope it does well', '2006-04-04 12:50:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2286262, 314898, 43463, '<td valign="top">The first thing I notice when I look upon the picture is this man''s gaze. He has this penetrating gaze that just arrests you. You managed to capture that exceptionally well. As this is the yellow challenge this composition would have been better had the man been leaning on the yellow tractor instead of that off camera orange one. His stance is great, but I would have prefered it not to be obscuring the yellow tractor nor the grille of the tractor. As the viewer, let us see more of the tools of his trade - show us more don''t obscure it. The face of this gentleman has lots of character and the composition would have more visual impact if it was taken as a middle portrait shot - mainly from the waist up so as to draw more focus onto the individual and even less on the surrounding background.</td>', 'The first thing I notice when I look upon the picture is this man''s gaze. He has this penetrating gaze that just arrests you. You managed to capture that exceptionally well. As this is the yellow challenge this composition would have been better had the man been leaning on the yellow tractor instead of that off camera orange one. His stance is great, but I would have prefered it not to be obscuring the yellow tractor nor the grille of the tractor. As the viewer, let us see more of the tools of his trade - show us more don''t obscure it. The face of this gentleman has lots of character and the composition would have more visual impact if it was taken as a middle portrait shot - mainly from the waist up so as to draw more focus onto the individual and even less on the surrounding background.', '2006-04-04 12:57:16.000000', NULL, 1),
