(2300753, 313276, 30982, '<td valign="top">I really like how the glass seems to almost disappear where it curves.  I think the one thing that did bother me was the way the line at the top curves, due to the glass curvature.  And I will admit, I am a bit tired of these, but I do think you did a pretty good job of it just the same.</td>', 'I really like how the glass seems to almost disappear where it curves.  I think the one thing that did bother me was the way the line at the top curves, due to the glass curvature.  And I will admit, I am a bit tired of these, but I do think you did a pretty good job of it just the same.', '2006-04-10 02:48:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2300755, 312429, 43434, '<td valign="top">Ok I didn''t need to know about the boxers on the head .. but a good front page image really.</td>', 'Ok I didn''t need to know about the boxers on the head .. but a good front page image really.', '2006-04-10 02:48:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2300763, 314487, 31443, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Well done!</td>', 'Congratulations! Well done!', '2006-04-10 02:51:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2300767, 312848, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh - this is way cuter than mine, that''s for sure! <br/> <br/>I LOVE the expression, and it works very well for the challenge - ie sunny disposition to go with the "yellow" jammies.  I realize that moving the person out of the middle is generally more pleasing, but he''s too close to the right for me.  Just a hair to the left would have made the diff (maybe).  The only other constructive crit I can offer is maybe, even though you''re a bit gunshy on the post-processing, is to "pop" it a bit more.  See what happens if you set the whites of the eyes on SpongeBob as pure white, for instance.  But the most important thing is it''s a wonderful shot of your kid!</td>', 'Heh - this is way cuter than mine, that''s for sure!  I LOVE the expression, and it works very well for the challenge - ie sunny disposition to go with the "yellow" jammies.  I realize that moving the person out of the middle is generally more pleasing, but he''s too close to the right for me.  Just a hair to the left would have made the diff (maybe).  The only other constructive crit I can offer is maybe, even though you''re a bit gunshy on the post-processing, is to "pop" it a bit more.  See what happens if you set the whites of the eyes on SpongeBob as pure white, for instance.  But the most important thing is it''s a wonderful shot of your kid!', '2006-04-10 02:55:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2300768, 313900, 28710, '<td valign="top">Fun picture with that yellow in the bridge. I am a little uncomfortable about the angle of the bridge against the horizon although it''s not specifically bad.<br/> <br/>I would have tried to pull a bit of yellow out of the surrounding areas. The river and grass also appear to be quite yellow. I wouldn''t desaturate all the way, maybe -10 or -20?<br/> <br/>Congrats on beating my Tweety!</td>', 'Fun picture with that yellow in the bridge. I am a little uncomfortable about the angle of the bridge against the horizon although it''s not specifically bad. I would have tried to pull a bit of yellow out of the surrounding areas. The river and grass also appear to be quite yellow. I wouldn''t desaturate all the way, maybe -10 or -20? Congrats on beating my Tweety!', '2006-04-10 02:57:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2300770, 315648, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is a very pleasing image - nice color, nice composition as well.  What post processing software are you using?  With the 20D, you shouldn''t be seeing that much grain, I''d not think, unless it was a very small portion of the total image.</td>', 'This is a very pleasing image - nice color, nice composition as well.  What post processing software are you using?  With the 20D, you shouldn''t be seeing that much grain, I''d not think, unless it was a very small portion of the total image.', '2006-04-10 03:00:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2300774, 313900, 30982, '<td valign="top">I liked this image because it was definitely different from a lot of the others in the challenge.  The yellow REALLY stands out, and that makes it very appropriate.  If you''re so inclined, it might be interesting to see it as a selective desaturation, with everything else grayed except the bridge.  As for composition, don''t know if it matters or not, but the bridge itself isn''t quite at a 1/3 line or a 1/2 line - which may account for why it feels "unbalanced" to some.</td>', 'I liked this image because it was definitely different from a lot of the others in the challenge.  The yellow REALLY stands out, and that makes it very appropriate.  If you''re so inclined, it might be interesting to see it as a selective desaturation, with everything else grayed except the bridge.  As for composition, don''t know if it matters or not, but the bridge itself isn''t quite at a 1/3 line or a 1/2 line - which may account for why it feels "unbalanced" to some.', '2006-04-10 03:05:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2300779, 315638, 31443, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! We were close, weren''t we? Both in scores and scenery :) lovely shot!</td>', 'Congratulations! We were close, weren''t we? Both in scores and scenery :) lovely shot!', '2006-04-10 03:09:22.000000', NULL, 0),
