(2302757, 315333, 30982, '<td valign="top">I thought this was quite funny and fairly well done for a picture of a cow in a field.  How to make it better?  Not sure - I think you did a good job with what you set out to do, and the post processing on the cow is quite good.</td>', 'I thought this was quite funny and fairly well done for a picture of a cow in a field.  How to make it better?  Not sure - I think you did a good job with what you set out to do, and the post processing on the cow is quite good.', '2006-04-10 23:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302760, 314703, 42456, '<td valign="top">At least it didn''t get dq''d...of course that could still happen.</td>', 'At least it didn''t get dq''d...of course that could still happen.', '2006-04-10 23:34:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302761, 315649, 30982, '<td valign="top">Maybe try this at one of those weird angles people seem to like, forming a diagonal across the frame?  I''m not big on the pics of women eating things, but they generally seem to do OK on average.  Like someone else already mentioned, maybe dress it up a bit with red lipstick, red nailpolish, and have her pulling a bit off the peep.  By the way, I liked the outtake quite a bit!</td>', 'Maybe try this at one of those weird angles people seem to like, forming a diagonal across the frame?  I''m not big on the pics of women eating things, but they generally seem to do OK on average.  Like someone else already mentioned, maybe dress it up a bit with red lipstick, red nailpolish, and have her pulling a bit off the peep.  By the way, I liked the outtake quite a bit!', '2006-04-10 23:35:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302764, 315107, 30982, '<td valign="top">I liked this one quite a bit Rachel, and honestly feel it should have socred higher.  It it not too dark to me at all - I tend to like things darker than the average DPC''er does, it seems.  It''s got a very rich and luxurious feel to it, and is one of the times I don''t mind the "spray it with water!" approach - it works well here.  Composition is excellent.</td>', 'I liked this one quite a bit Rachel, and honestly feel it should have socred higher.  It it not too dark to me at all - I tend to like things darker than the average DPC''er does, it seems.  It''s got a very rich and luxurious feel to it, and is one of the times I don''t mind the "spray it with water!" approach - it works well here.  Composition is excellent.', '2006-04-10 23:40:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302765, 313606, 50641, '<td valign="top">Aw shit, I was one of your 7''s.  I like the idea, I like that you had AN IDEA, and I think harsh lighting is appropriate for a Lemonator. Context is important. I hope you keep decide to keep shooting what you want to shoot.  Don''t just take pictures that please the blandness of the masses. Please yourself and please the artist and comedian in you.  Cough   ...fuggem  :D</td>', 'Aw shit, I was one of your 7''s.  I like the idea, I like that you had AN IDEA, and I think harsh lighting is appropriate for a Lemonator. Context is important. I hope you keep decide to keep shooting what you want to shoot.  Don''t just take pictures that please the blandness of the masses. Please yourself and please the artist and comedian in you.  Cough   ...fuggem  :D', '2006-04-10 23:41:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302766, 315313, 30982, '<td valign="top">This one is appealing for a couple of reasons (to me, anyway) - the angle is different yet not disturbing, as moving things to an odd angle can be sometimes.  The tone of yellow and the composition are very "uplifting" creating a warm, cheeful type image.  And the "pink" adds an element of additional interest.  All that said, I think it needed a little less border, and a bit (just a bit!) more contrast, maybe.</td>', 'This one is appealing for a couple of reasons (to me, anyway) - the angle is different yet not disturbing, as moving things to an odd angle can be sometimes.  The tone of yellow and the composition are very "uplifting" creating a warm, cheeful type image.  And the "pink" adds an element of additional interest.  All that said, I think it needed a little less border, and a bit (just a bit!) more contrast, maybe.', '2006-04-10 23:44:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302769, 314252, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is an incredible shot!  The clarity and contrast in the black and white is exceptional - I''m really hoping you did one without the ducky to hang on the wall!  The addition of the ducky is nice to meet the challenge, and the use of color in just the duck works well for this shot.</td>', 'This is an incredible shot!  The clarity and contrast in the black and white is exceptional - I''m really hoping you did one without the ducky to hang on the wall!  The addition of the ducky is nice to meet the challenge, and the use of color in just the duck works well for this shot.', '2006-04-10 23:48:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302781, 315441, 30982, '<td valign="top">Not sure what to do to "make this better" - I think some have mentioned a dark background, but I think the use of a light background works well with your theme.  I really did like this when voting - still like it.  I think it''s very well done.</td>', 'Not sure what to do to "make this better" - I think some have mentioned a dark background, but I think the use of a light background works well with your theme.  I really did like this when voting - still like it.  I think it''s very well done.', '2006-04-10 23:51:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302867, 314769, 23394, '<td valign="top">yep, that''s a border ;-)</td>', 'yep, that''s a border ;-)', '2006-04-11 00:45:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302915, 314411, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''ll admit I missed the obvious play on words connection and I usually pay attention to titles after the initial viewing of the picture.  I do like the negative space and the bright lighting creeping around the side of Tweety''s head.  Reading your description, nice work using curves - the colors are spot on to me and the background is indeed quite black (which isn''t always the case.)  I thought it a unique take on the challenge and don''t agree with the number of scores 3 and below awarded here.  I will say that some don''t like the "corner" look - I don''t like it all the time - but it''s well justified here by your intent, and I thought it worked even though I missed the play on words.</td>', 'I''ll admit I missed the obvious play on words connection and I usually pay attention to titles after the initial viewing of the picture.  I do like the negative space and the bright lighting creeping around the side of Tweety''s head.  Reading your description, nice work using curves - the colors are spot on to me and the background is indeed quite black (which isn''t always the case.)  I thought it a unique take on the challenge and don''t agree with the number of scores 3 and below awarded here.  I will say that some don''t like the "corner" look - I don''t like it all the time - but it''s well justified here by your intent, and I thought it worked even though I missed the play on words.', '2006-04-11 01:17:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302941, 313343, 36377, '<td valign="top">That gradient was impossible. I kept moving the flashes to get it right and the glasses kept falling. That''s how I shattered the last one. <br/> <br/>One flash on either side pointed slightly up and in.</td>', 'That gradient was impossible. I kept moving the flashes to get it right and the glasses kept falling. That''s how I shattered the last one.  One flash on either side pointed slightly up and in.', '2006-04-11 01:39:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302950, 314769, 15711, '<td valign="top">Another one that was way underscored.  UGH what''s with the voters??</td>', 'Another one that was way underscored.  UGH what''s with the voters??', '2006-04-11 01:49:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302971, 314769, 19708, '<td valign="top">nah...<br/>was actually better than I expected.<br/> <br/>I could have used a classic<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=315041" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/315041.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/315041.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/315041.jpg"/></a> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=315039" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/315039.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/315039.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/315039.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>but has been done too many times.</td>', 'nah...was actually better than I expected. I could have used a classic   but has been done too many times.', '2006-04-11 02:06:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2302980, 313868, 37893, '<td valign="top">The idea here Jacque is a good one. However, there isn''t enough punch in the image. The WB seems a tad off and a tighter crop would have served this image a lot better.</td>', 'The idea here Jacque is a good one. However, there isn''t enough punch in the image. The WB seems a tad off and a tighter crop would have served this image a lot better.', '2006-04-11 02:24:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303032, 315307, 54540, '<td valign="top">Fantastic color combination, expecially with the background well out of the DOF!  Superb!</td>', 'Fantastic color combination, expecially with the background well out of the DOF!  Superb!', '2006-04-11 02:55:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303038, 314547, 41337, '<td valign="top">Strong image. Better luck next time!</td>', 'Strong image. Better luck next time!', '2006-04-11 02:59:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303078, 314547, 45003, '<td valign="top">Wow, that''s a compliment, Jutilda. Don''t know what to say. Thanks both!</td>', 'Wow, that''s a compliment, Jutilda. Don''t know what to say. Thanks both!', '2006-04-11 04:18:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303096, 314547, 37779, '<td valign="top">I can''t even believe the idiots called photographers on this site sometimes. This was a million times better than most of the top 10 and if they couldn''t see the yellow in it...they are enormously blind. You are really an amazing photog, and I really look forward to you kicking everyones trash on this site in the weeks to come. <br/>THANK YOU for this excellent submission that the poor souls of DPC missed out on with their stuck inside the box thinking.</td>', 'I can''t even believe the idiots called photographers on this site sometimes. This was a million times better than most of the top 10 and if they couldn''t see the yellow in it...they are enormously blind. You are really an amazing photog, and I really look forward to you kicking everyones trash on this site in the weeks to come. THANK YOU for this excellent submission that the poor souls of DPC missed out on with their stuck inside the box thinking.', '2006-04-11 04:49:20.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2303157, 314487, 47294, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i> Why does Rikki even think he has a chance in these things?  You are on fire GIS...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I don''t know, I think he is just a glutton for punishment!  Seriously though, Rikki has had some bad luck and challenged me twice when I was lucky enough to peak.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i>BTW, one more good one and you''ll have that coveted 6.0 average vote. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I know this will sound pretty childish to some DPC members but the 6 average is almost as important to me as winning a ribbon.  I currently have a photo in Textures which is sitting on 6.2 so if all goes to plan, I''ll finally have that 6 average after 35 challenges!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-11 05:49:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo: Why does Rikki even think he has a chance in these things?  You are on fire GIS...  I don''t know, I think he is just a glutton for punishment!  Seriously though, Rikki has had some bad luck and challenged me twice when I was lucky enough to peak. Originally posted by DrAchoo:BTW, one more good one and you''ll have that coveted 6.0 average vote.   I know this will sound pretty childish to some DPC members but the 6 average is almost as important to me as winning a ribbon.  I currently have a photo in Textures which is sitting on 6.2 so if all goes to plan, I''ll finally have that 6 average after 35 challenges!!!', '2006-04-11 06:48:55.000000', '2006-04-11 06:49:53.000000', 0),
(2303167, 315307, 23456, '<td valign="top">Simply WOW ! I can''t fault it. Congratulations !</td>', 'Simply WOW ! I can''t fault it. Congratulations !', '2006-04-11 07:00:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303168, 315590, 23456, '<td valign="top">WOW Simply fantastic. Easily a blue as well. Congratulations !</td>', 'WOW Simply fantastic. Easily a blue as well. Congratulations !', '2006-04-11 07:02:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303182, 315783, 38509, '<td valign="top">well, i was one of the 10 voters, i got the picture (photo) ;-)<br/> <br/>LOL</td>', 'well, i was one of the 10 voters, i got the picture (photo) ;-) LOL', '2006-04-11 07:43:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303196, 315208, 5728, '<td valign="top">The German name for the fruit is pampelmuse which translates to grapefruit, shaddock or pomelo. I translated to grapefruit in the title although it is more in the line of a shaddock I guess which are smaller than grapefruit but a lot smaller. The juice is in fact orange juice, which I chose because orange juice itself is yellow and not orange.<br/> <br/>Thanks for all your votes and comments.</td>', 'The German name for the fruit is pampelmuse which translates to grapefruit, shaddock or pomelo. I translated to grapefruit in the title although it is more in the line of a shaddock I guess which are smaller than grapefruit but a lot smaller. The juice is in fact orange juice, which I chose because orange juice itself is yellow and not orange. Thanks for all your votes and comments.', '2006-04-11 08:03:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303203, 313276, 42198, '<td valign="top">Nice use of lines and reflections/refractions, good composition. Works well as a vertical layout, which helps to draw the eye along the stem of the glass, and follow that line from top to bottom.<br/> <br/>It''d be good if the yellow was just a little bit brighter, and a bit... yellower!</td>', 'Nice use of lines and reflections/refractions, good composition. Works well as a vertical layout, which helps to draw the eye along the stem of the glass, and follow that line from top to bottom. It''d be good if the yellow was just a little bit brighter, and a bit... yellower!', '2006-04-11 08:11:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303209, 315565, 42198, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure what ''Strong'' means in this context, or what ''LiveStrong'' means, or even who Lance Armstrong is! - So apologies for that. I can only comment on the technicals of the shot.<br/> <br/>The lighting is fine, lit from the left with the rose pointing towards the light. Slight shadow falling across the jersey, but not so much to be distracting.<br/> <br/>The main thing that doesn''t sit well with me are the lines in the shot. Although the composition is fine in relation to the ''outside'' frame, the lines on the jersey add a very strong framing element to the shot, which kind of puts everything else off-balance. There''s a black line directly across the middle, and a strong black line down the right hand side, with nothing to balance it on the left.<br/> <br/>For me, the word ''Strong'' becomes the primary subject, with the yellow rose secondary.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-11 10:38:30.</i></td>', 'I''m not sure what ''Strong'' means in this context, or what ''LiveStrong'' means, or even who Lance Armstrong is! - So apologies for that. I can only comment on the technicals of the shot. The lighting is fine, lit from the left with the rose pointing towards the light. Slight shadow falling across the jersey, but not so much to be distracting. The main thing that doesn''t sit well with me are the lines in the shot. Although the composition is fine in relation to the ''outside'' frame, the lines on the jersey add a very strong framing element to the shot, which kind of puts everything else off-balance. There''s a black line directly across the middle, and a strong black line down the right hand side, with nothing to balance it on the left. For me, the word ''Strong'' becomes the primary subject, with the yellow rose secondary.', '2006-04-11 08:23:44.000000', '2006-04-11 11:38:30.000000', 0),
(2303218, 313844, 45521, '<td valign="top">Hey... I have the exact same car... It''s a saturn, 2001... the only year they made them yellow...<br/>I like the picture by the way...</td>', 'Hey... I have the exact same car... It''s a saturn, 2001... the only year they made them yellow...I like the picture by the way...', '2006-04-11 08:39:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303222, 313900, 42198, '<td valign="top">Nice bright vivid yellow, and an interesting subject - not very often you see bridges this colour!<br/> <br/>However, even with that bright yellow bridge cutting across the middle of the shot, the lines and composition actually draw my eye to the tree on the right. If you look at the lines, the river bank and the bridge are almost ''pointing'' at the tree (which itself is sitting on a thirds line)<br/> <br/>Good post processing, brought out the contrast well, and made the grey sky look interesting.</td>', 'Nice bright vivid yellow, and an interesting subject - not very often you see bridges this colour! However, even with that bright yellow bridge cutting across the middle of the shot, the lines and composition actually draw my eye to the tree on the right. If you look at the lines, the river bank and the bridge are almost ''pointing'' at the tree (which itself is sitting on a thirds line) Good post processing, brought out the contrast well, and made the grey sky look interesting.', '2006-04-11 08:52:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303249, 313868, 28710, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, but there are some serious fatal flaws that I see in this pic.<br/> <br/>#1 Focus. I would personally have used a deeper DOF to get more flowers in focus as well as keeping all parts of that vase sharp. Nice decorative work on it.<br/> <br/>#2 Depth of Frame. I think you could have greatly benefited by moving your whole setup about a half foot to a full foot farther away from the wall. This would have greatly helped in making the top part of the background Black as Black and would also put it in the defocused area. This might have helped if there was a problem with the actual graininess on the backdrop material.<br/> <br/>#3 Backdrops. Ooof. To be honest, I prefer the softer yellow of the cloth at the bottom of the frame over the yellow paper. Would there have been a way to set up the yellow cloth in such a way that it ''bent'' upwards as it went back to allow a totally fluid and seamless backdrop? You could then have used the black paper to create a nice flat line across the top. This would have been challenging as you would have needed to light the background. One idea would be to have a light stuck through the cloth and hidden behind the carnations. It would have had a nice, balanced effect. It still would have needed a bit of side lighting to give depth and definition to the carnations, but that would have been OK because the subject would have been moved away from the backdrop.. right?<br/> <br/>#4 Blacks. I felt that the main idea of this picture was to allow the top of the black vase to meld seamlessly into the background when I first saw the thumbnail. Doesn''t look like it worked out so well here.<br/> <br/>If you got the lighting right and moved the flowers/vase forwards, you would likely have found that your actual Background was quite black already (keep that backlighting LOW). This would have made it easier to hit curves and meld away.<br/> <br/>I really like the idea of a vase that looks like a drip from the blackness coming to form a glass object with flowers sticking out of it.<br/> <br/>It was a great idea.</td>', 'I like the idea, but there are some serious fatal flaws that I see in this pic. #1 Focus. I would personally have used a deeper DOF to get more flowers in focus as well as keeping all parts of that vase sharp. Nice decorative work on it. #2 Depth of Frame. I think you could have greatly benefited by moving your whole setup about a half foot to a full foot farther away from the wall. This would have greatly helped in making the top part of the background Black as Black and would also put it in the defocused area. This might have helped if there was a problem with the actual graininess on the backdrop material. #3 Backdrops. Ooof. To be honest, I prefer the softer yellow of the cloth at the bottom of the frame over the yellow paper. Would there have been a way to set up the yellow cloth in such a way that it ''bent'' upwards as it went back to allow a totally fluid and seamless backdrop? You could then have used the black paper to create a nice flat line across the top. This would have been challenging as you would have needed to light the background. One idea would be to have a light stuck through the cloth and hidden behind the carnations. It would have had a nice, balanced effect. It still would have needed a bit of side lighting to give depth and definition to the carnations, but that would have been OK because the subject would have been moved away from the backdrop.. right? #4 Blacks. I felt that the main idea of this picture was to allow the top of the black vase to meld seamlessly into the background when I first saw the thumbnail. Doesn''t look like it worked out so well here. If you got the lighting right and moved the flowers/vase forwards, you would likely have found that your actual Background was quite black already (keep that backlighting LOW). This would have made it easier to hit curves and meld away. I really like the idea of a vase that looks like a drip from the blackness coming to form a glass object with flowers sticking out of it. It was a great idea.', '2006-04-11 09:14:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303252, 314363, 28710, '<td valign="top">Fantastic. It''s a little rough in spots in the fore lamp, but otherwise, it kicks keester!</td>', 'Fantastic. It''s a little rough in spots in the fore lamp, but otherwise, it kicks keester!', '2006-04-11 09:16:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303256, 313276, 28710, '<td valign="top">I just looked at just the top third/half and it looks like a face with Rasta (Ganja) eyes and a MONSTER afro. This could have been an interesting variant...<br/> <br/>I think the glass is your greatest obstacle in this pic. When I did my first glass picture, I was surprised at how low the quality is in glassware. Man, when is Canon going to come out with some L series goblets, snifters and other assorted wine glasses?</td>', 'I just looked at just the top third/half and it looks like a face with Rasta (Ganja) eyes and a MONSTER afro. This could have been an interesting variant... I think the glass is your greatest obstacle in this pic. When I did my first glass picture, I was surprised at how low the quality is in glassware. Man, when is Canon going to come out with some L series goblets, snifters and other assorted wine glasses?', '2006-04-11 09:19:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303270, 312848, 28710, '<td valign="top">Good use of fifths. It''s still a bit to the right, but it''s pretty close.<br/> <br/>Only complaint from me is that it seems a tiny bit too soft (mostly in the hand) and there''s a nasty mark in the BG. <br/> <br/>A crop in about 10-15% might have righted the composition (this far to the right almost suggests movement to the right to my eye, but this isn''t supported by the picture) and lost the hand. It might have looked a bit weird to have sliced them off, but then it draws the attention to the mirrored faces. Tough call. I don''t hate the current crop.<br/> <br/>Nice job.</td>', 'Good use of fifths. It''s still a bit to the right, but it''s pretty close. Only complaint from me is that it seems a tiny bit too soft (mostly in the hand) and there''s a nasty mark in the BG.  A crop in about 10-15% might have righted the composition (this far to the right almost suggests movement to the right to my eye, but this isn''t supported by the picture) and lost the hand. It might have looked a bit weird to have sliced them off, but then it draws the attention to the mirrored faces. Tough call. I don''t hate the current crop. Nice job.', '2006-04-11 09:27:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303276, 315565, 28710, '<td valign="top">Rose seems a bit soft... The jersey looks good.<br/> <br/>I was thinking that it would have been nice to have moved the rose up to the black strip to increase contrast and make it stand out more. Then I thought that it might have been fun to use the Rose as an ''R'', covering it with the head of the rose.<br/> <br/>The composition might have needed to change though with a slight turn to your right.<br/> <br/>This would be a fun picture to email to Lance!<br/> <br/>Ride on sista!</td>', 'Rose seems a bit soft... The jersey looks good. I was thinking that it would have been nice to have moved the rose up to the black strip to increase contrast and make it stand out more. Then I thought that it might have been fun to use the Rose as an ''R'', covering it with the head of the rose. The composition might have needed to change though with a slight turn to your right. This would be a fun picture to email to Lance! Ride on sista!', '2006-04-11 09:30:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303289, 314487, 43503, '<td valign="top">It''s fantastic!well done!I wish I was there at this very moment with a medium format camera to capture the left square part of the image!</td>', 'It''s fantastic!well done!I wish I was there at this very moment with a medium format camera to capture the left square part of the image!', '2006-04-11 09:52:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303328, 314252, 28710, '<td valign="top">What a fun picture. Seriously. I just wish that there wasn''t such a strong bias against the venerable Rubber Ducky who has put in such service on this website and in photography in general. Might have been a fun picture with something else, but what would have been yellow?<br/> <br/>Nice shot.</td>', 'What a fun picture. Seriously. I just wish that there wasn''t such a strong bias against the venerable Rubber Ducky who has put in such service on this website and in photography in general. Might have been a fun picture with something else, but what would have been yellow? Nice shot.', '2006-04-11 10:25:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303329, 315441, 28710, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. Gratz on 0 1''s. I dig the way the end of the finger seems brighter. Well done.<br/> <br/>EDIT Oh yeah, fabulous detail on the hand. Perfect. As one would expect for the hand of God... ;)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-11 09:28:20.</i></td>', 'Nice shot. Gratz on 0 1''s. I dig the way the end of the finger seems brighter. Well done. EDIT Oh yeah, fabulous detail on the hand. Perfect. As one would expect for the hand of God... ;)', '2006-04-11 10:27:25.000000', '2006-04-11 10:28:20.000000', 0),
(2303336, 315313, 28710, '<td valign="top">Love the title. Enjoyed the execution of the shot. My only real gripe is that the border could have stood to be a tiny bit brighter....<br/> <br/>and the rest of the shot a little sharper...<br/> <br/>And some of the reflections were softer on the far side of the pot.<br/> <br/>Otherwise fantastic!</td>', 'Love the title. Enjoyed the execution of the shot. My only real gripe is that the border could have stood to be a tiny bit brighter.... and the rest of the shot a little sharper... And some of the reflections were softer on the far side of the pot. Otherwise fantastic!', '2006-04-11 10:30:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303339, 315333, 28710, '<td valign="top">It definitely has the "spy camera" look.<br/> <br/>Not sure if the spy camera look is really the best medium to score points...<br/> <br/>I''m concerned that if I say it''s soft and the colors are a bit weak (grass, weeds, yellow in the cow), you might have put these features in there for effect.<br/> <br/>It''s a fun picture though and I do actually like it.</td>', 'It definitely has the "spy camera" look. Not sure if the spy camera look is really the best medium to score points... I''m concerned that if I say it''s soft and the colors are a bit weak (grass, weeds, yellow in the cow), you might have put these features in there for effect. It''s a fun picture though and I do actually like it.', '2006-04-11 10:33:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303340, 315714, 42125, '<td valign="top">You keep getting higher scores!<br/>Congratulations on your highest again :-)<br/> <br/>Edited: Forgot to tell you that this is a very good photograph. To bad though that the windows are black! Are they sealed?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-11 09:34:50.</i></td>', 'You keep getting higher scores!Congratulations on your highest again :-) Edited: Forgot to tell you that this is a very good photograph. To bad though that the windows are black! Are they sealed?', '2006-04-11 10:33:17.000000', '2006-04-11 10:34:50.000000', 0),
(2303353, 315649, 28710, '<td valign="top">Easter Eater?<br/> <br/>I don''t know what those are, but they look like they are either really yummy or really nasty.<br/> <br/>I like how the middle one has a little speck reminiscent of a small circle for the mouth. As if it''s surprised/worried about the prospect of being the next one down the hatch...<br/> <br/>I''m sorry to say this, but I honestly don''t like the picture.<br/> <br/>The lighting, the model''s make-up (POWDER!), messy yellow stuff everywhere, uninteresting hands and general composition are disappointing to me.<br/> <br/>Using a white background might have helped to hide some things (like the lip-hair, which I might add is NOT considered unattractive in every culture, it''s quite a mark of beauty in the philippines and some other asian countries, but in those cases, they like it more off on the sides) and softened the harshness of this rather stark picture.<br/> <br/>Further, balancing the light would have REALLY helped this. Generally speaking, using the flash as a primary light source is a BIG no-no.<br/> <br/>I''m not trying to be harsh here, just specific.</td>', 'Easter Eater? I don''t know what those are, but they look like they are either really yummy or really nasty. I like how the middle one has a little speck reminiscent of a small circle for the mouth. As if it''s surprised/worried about the prospect of being the next one down the hatch... I''m sorry to say this, but I honestly don''t like the picture. The lighting, the model''s make-up (POWDER!), messy yellow stuff everywhere, uninteresting hands and general composition are disappointing to me. Using a white background might have helped to hide some things (like the lip-hair, which I might add is NOT considered unattractive in every culture, it''s quite a mark of beauty in the philippines and some other asian countries, but in those cases, they like it more off on the sides) and softened the harshness of this rather stark picture. Further, balancing the light would have REALLY helped this. Generally speaking, using the flash as a primary light source is a BIG no-no. I''m not trying to be harsh here, just specific.', '2006-04-11 10:41:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303423, 314411, 42198, '<td valign="top">I really like this, and think it was underrated - I thought it would have scored at least a 5.0<br/> <br/>The composition and the simplicity work very well, I like the black background which helps the yellow stand out.<br/> <br/>The only technical flaw I can see is the bright light coming in from the right. This causes a highlight which is a bit distracting.<br/> <br/>Oh, I only realised this was tweety when I read your comments! - I originally thought this was a rubber duck.</td>', 'I really like this, and think it was underrated - I thought it would have scored at least a 5.0 The composition and the simplicity work very well, I like the black background which helps the yellow stand out. The only technical flaw I can see is the bright light coming in from the right. This causes a highlight which is a bit distracting. Oh, I only realised this was tweety when I read your comments! - I originally thought this was a rubber duck.', '2006-04-11 11:34:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303424, 315307, 44780, '<td valign="top">I also missed the voting.... but it''s a 10 for me!</td>', 'I also missed the voting.... but it''s a 10 for me!', '2006-04-11 11:37:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303572, 314974, 50641, '<td valign="top">I like this shot. My favorite part is the stems. It''s an interesting crop and the lighting is balanced. I really would have predicted this to score better.  I guess it''s just that darn gummy yellow that softens the definition... for everyone shooting yellows.  I propose a toast to yellowlessness, for a while anyway ;-)</td>', 'I like this shot. My favorite part is the stems. It''s an interesting crop and the lighting is balanced. I really would have predicted this to score better.  I guess it''s just that darn gummy yellow that softens the definition... for everyone shooting yellows.  I propose a toast to yellowlessness, for a while anyway ;-)', '2006-04-11 13:01:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303588, 314788, 24642, '<td valign="top">Til lukku með árangurinn Gurry.  Besta myndin að mínu mati.</td>', 'Til lukku með árangurinn Gurry.  Besta myndin að mínu mati.', '2006-04-11 13:09:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303728, 315565, 43148, '<td valign="top">Think most has been said, only thing I could think of to try is along the lines of what eschelar said, but I would TRY to make the rose to "O" in S T R (Rose) N G, not sure if it could be done, but maybe if done well, would have increased your score a lot. My opinion, we understand! LOL<br/> <br/>Jacque</td>', 'Think most has been said, only thing I could think of to try is along the lines of what eschelar said, but I would TRY to make the rose to "O" in S T R (Rose) N G, not sure if it could be done, but maybe if done well, would have increased your score a lot. My opinion, we understand! LOL Jacque', '2006-04-11 14:34:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303729, 315714, 26045, '<td valign="top"><br/> <br/>Hey grrrly! Way to beat your own top scorer!! :)<br/> <br/></td>', ' Hey grrrly! Way to beat your own top scorer!! :) ', '2006-04-11 14:35:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303740, 315333, 43148, '<td valign="top">Apologies, in advance!!<br/> <br/>First, so as not to cow tow to you, this could have been an udder disaster, but you horned in and milked it for all it was worth! Now hope you do not get de-fence-ive, but you must  weed  through all the comments and squeeze out the good ones!<br/> <br/>Actually, I really think you did a good job on this, missed a couple small white spots on cow, but that may be natural??? LOL. May trying to crop the photo different, getting the cow on maybe the lower left third line? Think that may give it a bit more pizazz, this is of course, MY OPINION&lt; only.. LOL<br/> <br/>Jacque</td>', 'Apologies, in advance!! First, so as not to cow tow to you, this could have been an udder disaster, but you horned in and milked it for all it was worth! Now hope you do not get de-fence-ive, but you must  weed  through all the comments and squeeze out the good ones! Actually, I really think you did a good job on this, missed a couple small white spots on cow, but that may be natural??? LOL. May trying to crop the photo different, getting the cow on maybe the lower left third line? Think that may give it a bit more pizazz, this is of course, MY OPINION< only.. LOL Jacque', '2006-04-11 14:40:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303745, 315441, 43148, '<td valign="top">I skipped voting on this one, sorry, though it is technically very nicely done, I did NOT like it. So, as I refuse to give a good image that meets the challenge a low score, I just skip them, wish others would do the same, btw!! Anyway, FIRST thing I thought of when this photo came up during voting was "E T ripoff", understand that it very well may not be, but that is all I saw in it. I am sorry that I do not like it, but..... people are different. AND, I do say, it is WELL done!<br/> <br/>Jacque</td>', 'I skipped voting on this one, sorry, though it is technically very nicely done, I did NOT like it. So, as I refuse to give a good image that meets the challenge a low score, I just skip them, wish others would do the same, btw!! Anyway, FIRST thing I thought of when this photo came up during voting was "E T ripoff", understand that it very well may not be, but that is all I saw in it. I am sorry that I do not like it, but..... people are different. AND, I do say, it is WELL done! Jacque', '2006-04-11 14:44:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303808, 315673, 70, '<td valign="top">Hey Melissa - this is a definite improvement over your other entry, the contrast looks much better. Looks like maybe you oversaturated the yellows just a bit because the legs are looking kind of yellowy (or maybe you''re jaundiced?) Good luck on your next entry. :)</td>', 'Hey Melissa - this is a definite improvement over your other entry, the contrast looks much better. Looks like maybe you oversaturated the yellows just a bit because the legs are looking kind of yellowy (or maybe you''re jaundiced?) Good luck on your next entry. :)', '2006-04-11 15:14:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303890, 313868, 42198, '<td valign="top">Most of what eschelar said below were also my thoughts on the technical aspects.<br/> <br/>My only additional technical observation is that it would have been good to bring out the colours and contrast (especially the contrast) in post-processing. The lighting looks a bit flat, so post-processing would have made the contrast and tones more interesting.<br/> <br/>While this is a nice ''classic'' composition, it just lacks that extra something to hold my interest for very long. The most interesting part of the shot for me was the pattern on the vase.</td>', 'Most of what eschelar said below were also my thoughts on the technical aspects. My only additional technical observation is that it would have been good to bring out the colours and contrast (especially the contrast) in post-processing. The lighting looks a bit flat, so post-processing would have made the contrast and tones more interesting. While this is a nice ''classic'' composition, it just lacks that extra something to hold my interest for very long. The most interesting part of the shot for me was the pattern on the vase.', '2006-04-11 15:50:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303897, 314809, 43405, '<td valign="top">Ha, I knew it :) Memory not bad huh?<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=291565" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/446/thumb/291565.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/446/thumb/291565.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/446/thumb/291565.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Ha, I knew it :) Memory not bad huh? ', '2006-04-11 15:54:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303898, 314363, 42198, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot, really holds my attention. Mostly because I''m trying to figure out how you did it, and what the setup was!<br/> <br/>I assume it''s three lava lamps positioned in a dark room? - If so then you did a good job of controlling the lighting to ensure that only the insides of the lamps were illuminated. A great idea with good visual impact, and you executed it well.<br/> <br/>The composition really adds to this, and technically I can''t find anything wrong with it.</td>', 'This is a great shot, really holds my attention. Mostly because I''m trying to figure out how you did it, and what the setup was! I assume it''s three lava lamps positioned in a dark room? - If so then you did a good job of controlling the lighting to ensure that only the insides of the lamps were illuminated. A great idea with good visual impact, and you executed it well. The composition really adds to this, and technically I can''t find anything wrong with it.', '2006-04-11 15:54:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303906, 312848, 42198, '<td valign="top">You captured a great shot here - I really like his expression.<br/> <br/>Two things caught my attention on the technical side; The white balance looks wrong, it has a feeling of being too ''warm'' like it was shot under incandescent light. Also the crop is a bit strange around his thighs. It''s an unusual place to chop him off!<br/> <br/>But, I like the simplicity of this.</td>', 'You captured a great shot here - I really like his expression. Two things caught my attention on the technical side; The white balance looks wrong, it has a feeling of being too ''warm'' like it was shot under incandescent light. Also the crop is a bit strange around his thighs. It''s an unusual place to chop him off! But, I like the simplicity of this.', '2006-04-11 15:58:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303919, 315649, 42198, '<td valign="top">I''m finding this one really tough to comment on. I don''t know what that yellow thing she''s eating is, some sort of marshmallow? It looks interesting whatever it is!<br/> <br/>But what distracts me more than anything is that it has a certain snapshot look about it. And, for me, what gives it that feel is the lighting. It really looks like you used on-camera flash here, I could be wrong, but that''s the feeling I get.</td>', 'I''m finding this one really tough to comment on. I don''t know what that yellow thing she''s eating is, some sort of marshmallow? It looks interesting whatever it is! But what distracts me more than anything is that it has a certain snapshot look about it. And, for me, what gives it that feel is the lighting. It really looks like you used on-camera flash here, I could be wrong, but that''s the feeling I get.', '2006-04-11 16:03:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303928, 315333, 42198, '<td valign="top">I''ve come back to this one a few times, but I really like it and think it should have at least broken a 5.0!<br/> <br/>It''s a really imaginative shot, and works very well.<br/> <br/>The only technical suggestions I can think of are; Tighter crop around the cow. Shooting at a different time of day to get more interesting lighting/shadows on the grass. Focus.</td>', 'I''ve come back to this one a few times, but I really like it and think it should have at least broken a 5.0! It''s a really imaginative shot, and works very well. The only technical suggestions I can think of are; Tighter crop around the cow. Shooting at a different time of day to get more interesting lighting/shadows on the grass. Focus.', '2006-04-11 16:07:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303930, 313868, 43148, '<td valign="top">That vase has been mentioned a couple of times, it is a Tiffin Glass Satin Finished black glass vase with Rockwell Sterling overlay. One of our favorite black glass pieces, we have over 100. Chose the satin finish as has almost no reflective problems, as most other glass does. Easy to use even a flash and get no bad spots with it!! Small tip that does work! LOL<br/> <br/>Jacque</td>', 'That vase has been mentioned a couple of times, it is a Tiffin Glass Satin Finished black glass vase with Rockwell Sterling overlay. One of our favorite black glass pieces, we have over 100. Chose the satin finish as has almost no reflective problems, as most other glass does. Easy to use even a flash and get no bad spots with it!! Small tip that does work! LOL Jacque', '2006-04-11 16:08:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303959, 315648, 42198, '<td valign="top">This almost has a ''35mm film'' feel about it. Nicely done. Something about the saturation and the grain in the purples.<br/> <br/>Good lighting and focus. I can''t really think of any suggestions to make on the technicals. Composition works well here to draw the eye to the centre of the flower.<br/> <br/>But I really like that background, the yellow and purple are beautiful together.</td>', 'This almost has a ''35mm film'' feel about it. Nicely done. Something about the saturation and the grain in the purples. Good lighting and focus. I can''t really think of any suggestions to make on the technicals. Composition works well here to draw the eye to the centre of the flower. But I really like that background, the yellow and purple are beautiful together.', '2006-04-11 16:23:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303969, 315441, 47117, '<td valign="top">I don''t know why, but the more I look at this the more I like it. Wish I had voted it higher then I did. At first glance it looks rather blah from the desat, but it really is quite interesting as I look at it more deeply. I feel that I just want that color to finally reach the flower so the flower would burst with it! Nicely done!!</td>', 'I don''t know why, but the more I look at this the more I like it. Wish I had voted it higher then I did. At first glance it looks rather blah from the desat, but it really is quite interesting as I look at it more deeply. I feel that I just want that color to finally reach the flower so the flower would burst with it! Nicely done!!', '2006-04-11 16:29:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2303998, 315194, 47117, '<td valign="top">Didn''t quite like it for the yellow challenge, but it is something I would hang on my kitchen wall. Terrific vintage feel to it. I would make it a print!</td>', 'Didn''t quite like it for the yellow challenge, but it is something I would hang on my kitchen wall. Terrific vintage feel to it. I would make it a print!', '2006-04-11 16:43:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304076, 315335, 43774, '<td valign="top">Pidge, I can''t believe this scored so low. I gave it a 9 and I really expected to see it on the first page.</td>', 'Pidge, I can''t believe this scored so low. I gave it a 9 and I really expected to see it on the first page.', '2006-04-11 17:16:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304126, 314547, 48954, '<td valign="top">4.8????? What a scandal!!!!! I mean really; gold is yellow! The idea is great and the execution is excellent. I''m telling you Arti-Elvi, some people on this site...welll, no comment. I cannot belive you got 4.8!?!</td>', '4.8????? What a scandal!!!!! I mean really; gold is yellow! The idea is great and the execution is excellent. I''m telling you Arti-Elvi, some people on this site...welll, no comment. I cannot belive you got 4.8!?!', '2006-04-11 17:36:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304140, 314547, 45003, '<td valign="top">Ah, how sweet of you guys. Thanks!</td>', 'Ah, how sweet of you guys. Thanks!', '2006-04-11 17:39:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304166, 312546, 42198, '<td valign="top">I like the black background here - It really sets it apart, and off-sets nicely against the main subject colours.<br/> <br/>Great use of repetition, with all of them looking the same direction and that lovely touch with the duckling on the bottom-left in mid-quack! Technicals are good, focus, lighting etc.<br/> <br/>Fitting title as well (now that I''ve looked it up)<br/> <br/>I have a feeling if they had been yellow all-over you''d be looking at a top ten finish.</td>', 'I like the black background here - It really sets it apart, and off-sets nicely against the main subject colours. Great use of repetition, with all of them looking the same direction and that lovely touch with the duckling on the bottom-left in mid-quack! Technicals are good, focus, lighting etc. Fitting title as well (now that I''ve looked it up) I have a feeling if they had been yellow all-over you''d be looking at a top ten finish.', '2006-04-11 17:51:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304182, 315785, 25397, '<td valign="top">:-Di feel the same about this</td>', ':-Di feel the same about this', '2006-04-11 18:00:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304219, 314529, 30808, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work. The yellow colored lines, inside a well treated B&amp;W seems very nice. Impressive angle also. I liked this one.</td>', 'Beautiful work. The yellow colored lines, inside a well treated B&W seems very nice. Impressive angle also. I liked this one.', '2006-04-11 18:25:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304232, 315785, 30861, '<td valign="top">You''re marginally certifiable, sheesh... This was one of my faves in the challenge. I''m way surprised it scored so low :-(</td>', 'You''re marginally certifiable, sheesh... This was one of my faves in the challenge. I''m way surprised it scored so low :-(', '2006-04-11 18:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304400, 315307, 54283, '<td valign="top">Bautiful shot. congratulations.<br/></td>', 'Bautiful shot. congratulations.', '2006-04-11 19:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304460, 314809, 46853, '<td valign="top">No your memory is fantastic.  I was a bit amazed that anyone would remember that shot.  and also from another view.  So I guess you have photographic memory.</td>', 'No your memory is fantastic.  I was a bit amazed that anyone would remember that shot.  and also from another view.  So I guess you have photographic memory.', '2006-04-11 20:16:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304575, 315151, 12448, '<td valign="top">Okay, didn''t get into a lot of detail the first time around so I''ll try to be a little more detailed this time around.<br/> <br/>I like the idea, the concept, the action.  But the colors on the car are as I said before, a bit dull and uninteresting overall.  Possibly a tweek to the levels or contrast could really make this shot stand out a bit more colorwise.  Also sine this was advance, maybe using a dodge tool set very lightly to really burn in the curves and corners might again really make this stand out more.  I really like the stop motion on the dirt and the car itself.  If you try any of these suggestions I would love to see the results.<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Okay, didn''t get into a lot of detail the first time around so I''ll try to be a little more detailed this time around. I like the idea, the concept, the action.  But the colors on the car are as I said before, a bit dull and uninteresting overall.  Possibly a tweek to the levels or contrast could really make this shot stand out a bit more colorwise.  Also sine this was advance, maybe using a dodge tool set very lightly to really burn in the curves and corners might again really make this stand out more.  I really like the stop motion on the dirt and the car itself.  If you try any of these suggestions I would love to see the results. Deannda', '2006-04-11 21:07:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304582, 315438, 12448, '<td valign="top">This is so cool!  I didn''t get to it during the challenge so didn''t get a chance to vote on it. There were too many, LOL :)<br/> <br/>I really like the colors, the clarity and the look of this shot.  The only thing that bothers me just a touch is the balance, the X on the rope isn''t on a third line or cross section or even in the middle on the side, it leaves me feeling a bit off for some reason.  Maybe just a slightly different crop?  Otherwise I cannot find anything wrong with this, I would have given it a 9 if I had gotten to it.<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'This is so cool!  I didn''t get to it during the challenge so didn''t get a chance to vote on it. There were too many, LOL :) I really like the colors, the clarity and the look of this shot.  The only thing that bothers me just a touch is the balance, the X on the rope isn''t on a third line or cross section or even in the middle on the side, it leaves me feeling a bit off for some reason.  Maybe just a slightly different crop?  Otherwise I cannot find anything wrong with this, I would have given it a 9 if I had gotten to it. Deannda', '2006-04-11 21:10:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304590, 313868, 33400, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition and layout here.  The only thing I think you could have done better, post process, would be to apply neat image or something like it to the top background.  The two color split, with contrasting top and bottom of the flowers and vase is excellent, but I''m distracted by the texture on top.<br/>You also have a little wrinkle on the yellow bottom near the left side of the vase, and the color on bottom could have been brightened a little with more direct lighting.<br/> <br/>I know, I know. You''ve seen my yellow entry, and who am I to say these things?!  But I really do like your shot and only want to offer what I see and have tried to learn myself.</td>', 'I really like the composition and layout here.  The only thing I think you could have done better, post process, would be to apply neat image or something like it to the top background.  The two color split, with contrasting top and bottom of the flowers and vase is excellent, but I''m distracted by the texture on top.You also have a little wrinkle on the yellow bottom near the left side of the vase, and the color on bottom could have been brightened a little with more direct lighting. I know, I know. You''ve seen my yellow entry, and who am I to say these things?!  But I really do like your shot and only want to offer what I see and have tried to learn myself.', '2006-04-11 21:14:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304605, 314363, 33400, '<td valign="top">Very cool.<br/>I want one of those.<br/> <br/>The composition here is great.  So are there three lava things? or are you very tricky with mirrors?  Honestly the only thing I think you could have improved is the focus on the left.<br/> <br/>I''m becoming a big fan of Neat Image and am wondering if it might have helped clean up some of the noise in the yellow areas -not really bad stuff, but it''s the only thing along with the focus that I can see to keep this from a really high score.  Good job.</td>', 'Very cool.I want one of those. The composition here is great.  So are there three lava things? or are you very tricky with mirrors?  Honestly the only thing I think you could have improved is the focus on the left. I''m becoming a big fan of Neat Image and am wondering if it might have helped clean up some of the noise in the yellow areas -not really bad stuff, but it''s the only thing along with the focus that I can see to keep this from a really high score.  Good job.', '2006-04-11 21:23:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304606, 314557, 12448, '<td valign="top">LOL!  I love the expression on the cow''s face, LOL!<br/> <br/>Okay, GREAT idea, original, unique and well composed.  So why did it not do better?  Well, my opinion, for what it''s worth (about 2 cents on EBay) is the cow is dull.  You desaturated the rest of the picture and not sure just how you went about it but the cow is dull and to me when a shot is desaturated the color part that is left out should really stand out.  I know some are very subtle and such but this just begs for a more vibrant color of Yellow, not literally sunshine yellow but more than what is showing.  Also, the line around the cow seems very percise, no give or take between it and the background.  Maybe a slight blur or feather the wand a bit to allow a little less rigidity?  Hope these comments help.<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'LOL!  I love the expression on the cow''s face, LOL! Okay, GREAT idea, original, unique and well composed.  So why did it not do better?  Well, my opinion, for what it''s worth (about 2 cents on EBay) is the cow is dull.  You desaturated the rest of the picture and not sure just how you went about it but the cow is dull and to me when a shot is desaturated the color part that is left out should really stand out.  I know some are very subtle and such but this just begs for a more vibrant color of Yellow, not literally sunshine yellow but more than what is showing.  Also, the line around the cow seems very percise, no give or take between it and the background.  Maybe a slight blur or feather the wand a bit to allow a little less rigidity?  Hope these comments help. Deannda', '2006-04-11 21:24:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304613, 314557, 12448, '<td valign="top">Oh and is the cow missing a leg?  I only see one front leg, looks a little odd, LOL :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh and is the cow missing a leg?  I only see one front leg, looks a little odd, LOL :) ', '2006-04-11 21:28:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304615, 313276, 33400, '<td valign="top">Well I like it.  There''s a reason for cliche''s.  People like certain things and this type of shot is one of them.<br/> <br/>There''s a little junk in the glass at the top on the right, and a few curvy areas in the stem and at the very top that probably distracted the voters.  The one thing I''ve noticed about these types of images is that the really good ones are near perfect symmetry.  The lines are straight, the sides balance each other perfectly etc.  I couldn''t do it. But then take a look at my yellow entry, then take this comment with a grain of salt :)<br/> <br/>Nice job.</td>', 'Well I like it.  There''s a reason for cliche''s.  People like certain things and this type of shot is one of them. There''s a little junk in the glass at the top on the right, and a few curvy areas in the stem and at the very top that probably distracted the voters.  The one thing I''ve noticed about these types of images is that the really good ones are near perfect symmetry.  The lines are straight, the sides balance each other perfectly etc.  I couldn''t do it. But then take a look at my yellow entry, then take this comment with a grain of salt :) Nice job.', '2006-04-11 21:29:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304644, 315441, 53147, '<td valign="top">I liked this one as it was not the typical flower shot. Not much I could add to make it "better" as I couldnt have done as well myself. The sharpness inthe hand and flower was good and I didn''t have an issue with the light background. I don''t believe a dark background would have given the same if not better effect. Nice job.</td>', 'I liked this one as it was not the typical flower shot. Not much I could add to make it "better" as I couldnt have done as well myself. The sharpness inthe hand and flower was good and I didn''t have an issue with the light background. I don''t believe a dark background would have given the same if not better effect. Nice job.', '2006-04-11 21:41:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304671, 314411, 53147, '<td valign="top">I really liked the use of the space to the right (my preference is to the left but what can you do - lol). I must admit I didnt get the reference in the title - but I don''t believe that is any reason to drop the score on a pic. This is a picture competition after all. I would have to agree with some of the others that Tweetys face is a bit flat and unfortunately didnt have more detail to it - not that his face has alot of detail in the first place - just seemed a bit too simple. I dont agree with the votes under 3 and I did have you scored higher than your average.</td>', 'I really liked the use of the space to the right (my preference is to the left but what can you do - lol). I must admit I didnt get the reference in the title - but I don''t believe that is any reason to drop the score on a pic. This is a picture competition after all. I would have to agree with some of the others that Tweetys face is a bit flat and unfortunately didnt have more detail to it - not that his face has alot of detail in the first place - just seemed a bit too simple. I dont agree with the votes under 3 and I did have you scored higher than your average.', '2006-04-11 21:47:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304680, 314252, 53147, '<td valign="top">Great shot. Great sharpness and detail and the selective sat works well. Great score especially considering the kid factor ( I wasnt as fortunate). And along with some of the other middling masses scores - those votes below 4 are just not appropriate. What are they voting on?</td>', 'Great shot. Great sharpness and detail and the selective sat works well. Great score especially considering the kid factor ( I wasnt as fortunate). And along with some of the other middling masses scores - those votes below 4 are just not appropriate. What are they voting on?', '2006-04-11 21:51:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304727, 315684, 35274, '<td valign="top">Thankyou for the comments and votes everyone! ^_^</td>', 'Thankyou for the comments and votes everyone! ^_^', '2006-04-11 22:10:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304841, 312848, 33400, '<td valign="top">I like kid shots.  Don''t worry about always pleasing the DPC crowd - they''re a fickle lot.  This is a nice shot and a great model.  Your background is actually pretty good for being just a wall - good light.  He''s a little off-focus below the middle, but his smile is really the point of the shot.  Nice job.</td>', 'I like kid shots.  Don''t worry about always pleasing the DPC crowd - they''re a fickle lot.  This is a nice shot and a great model.  Your background is actually pretty good for being just a wall - good light.  He''s a little off-focus below the middle, but his smile is really the point of the shot.  Nice job.', '2006-04-11 23:05:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304853, 315648, 33400, '<td valign="top">I really like the soft but colorful background.  The flower could stand to be a little sharper on the top edge, but that''s really hard for me to get so I can''t, unfortunately, say how to do it better.  Still this is a very pleasing image and meets the challenge very well without being <i>only</i> yellow</td>', 'I really like the soft but colorful background.  The flower could stand to be a little sharper on the top edge, but that''s really hard for me to get so I can''t, unfortunately, say how to do it better.  Still this is a very pleasing image and meets the challenge very well without being only yellow', '2006-04-11 23:08:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304864, 315307, 3039, '<td valign="top">Wonderful. Well deserved - 1st Place!</td>', 'Wonderful. Well deserved - 1st Place!', '2006-04-11 23:11:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304873, 313900, 33400, '<td valign="top">OK, I saw your outtakes in the forum before seeing this one - sorry. But I like all three very much.  The setting is peaceful and crisp.  This shot is not as serene Yellow Bridge II. It''s a little brighter, which in this case does not help.  On the other hand, the sky and the tree are beautiful and provide excellent balance.  You have taken a three wonderful shots. I think this should have finished higher than it did.</td>', 'OK, I saw your outtakes in the forum before seeing this one - sorry. But I like all three very much.  The setting is peaceful and crisp.  This shot is not as serene Yellow Bridge II. It''s a little brighter, which in this case does not help.  On the other hand, the sky and the tree are beautiful and provide excellent balance.  You have taken a three wonderful shots. I think this should have finished higher than it did.', '2006-04-11 23:13:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304880, 313713, 10818, '<td valign="top">Its a wonderful photo, great focus and color.<br/> <br/>Great shot !</td>', 'Its a wonderful photo, great focus and color. Great shot !', '2006-04-11 23:16:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304888, 315565, 33400, '<td valign="top">Very yellow and very crisp - mostly.  The rose, while beautiful does not have as good a focus as your jersey (?).  I think to make this shot pop, the rose should be a little brighter and sharper.  All in all though this is a pretty shot.  I like the subtle contrast between "Strong" and a delicate rose.  Nice idea.</td>', 'Very yellow and very crisp - mostly.  The rose, while beautiful does not have as good a focus as your jersey (?).  I think to make this shot pop, the rose should be a little brighter and sharper.  All in all though this is a pretty shot.  I like the subtle contrast between "Strong" and a delicate rose.  Nice idea.', '2006-04-11 23:17:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304898, 315333, 33400, '<td valign="top">Thirty years ago I took a picture of a cow in a field.  And ever since then my entire family, especially my mother-in-law, has assumed I have a thing for them.  I now have a huge collection of knick-knacks, stuffed animals, pictures, etc.  <br/> <br/>And my cow wasn''t nearly this good.<br/> <br/>Great color balance and the bored confidence of the animal rounds out the clever absurdity of being yellow.  I like it a lot.  you were robbed by the voters.</td>', 'Thirty years ago I took a picture of a cow in a field.  And ever since then my entire family, especially my mother-in-law, has assumed I have a thing for them.  I now have a huge collection of knick-knacks, stuffed animals, pictures, etc.   And my cow wasn''t nearly this good. Great color balance and the bored confidence of the animal rounds out the clever absurdity of being yellow.  I like it a lot.  you were robbed by the voters.', '2006-04-11 23:24:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304910, 315107, 33400, '<td valign="top">I''ve read a few of the other comments and your post about the shot.  And yes, there''s a little problem with the background, but honestly, it seems to fit the point of the shot.  This is a rainy day picture, so the sun is not bright and the daisy is sitting peacefully in the twilight.  I actually think yo could have darkened the one bright area around the petals just a bit to soften the appearance of flash.<br/>It''s a good shot and you clearly deserved to move on to the next round.<br/>Congratulations.</td>', 'I''ve read a few of the other comments and your post about the shot.  And yes, there''s a little problem with the background, but honestly, it seems to fit the point of the shot.  This is a rainy day picture, so the sun is not bright and the daisy is sitting peacefully in the twilight.  I actually think yo could have darkened the one bright area around the petals just a bit to soften the appearance of flash.It''s a good shot and you clearly deserved to move on to the next round.Congratulations.', '2006-04-11 23:30:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2304986, 315565, 41337, '<td valign="top">I think it was you who mentioned in my Yellow entry that you thought about shooting something similar. Well I thought about shooting something like your photo. Over where I live there are lots of cyclists who like to train on the road nearby my house and many of them have team jeresys with yellow in them. <br/> <br/>Nice pic btw and lets go Team Outcasts!</td>', 'I think it was you who mentioned in my Yellow entry that you thought about shooting something similar. Well I thought about shooting something like your photo. Over where I live there are lots of cyclists who like to train on the road nearby my house and many of them have team jeresys with yellow in them.  Nice pic btw and lets go Team Outcasts!', '2006-04-11 23:59:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2305582, 315307, 3837, '<td valign="top">Natural is best.  Congratulations on the blue for this yellow rose.  To share a little-known fact, the song, "The Yellow Rose of Texas" is about a mulata - ethnic term for female first generation of mixed european and african ancestry (not to be too rabbit-proof).</td>', 'Natural is best.  Congratulations on the blue for this yellow rose.  To share a little-known fact, the song, "The Yellow Rose of Texas" is about a mulata - ethnic term for female first generation of mixed european and african ancestry (not to be too rabbit-proof).', '2006-04-12 03:16:51.000000', NULL, 0),
