(2316431, 315375, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is a lovely image, the blues, the yellow on the boat, the crisp clear color and image lend itself very well.  The overall balance is also there, very well centered.<br/> <br/>It meets the challenge in that it has the yellow base for the boat but that''s about all that really jumps out as far as challenge requirements.  The yellow doesn''t dominate the picture nor does it just fade away.  To do better in this paricular challenge you might have desaturated the blue quite a bit to make the yellow stand out more.  But I really like the shot just as it is, a very nice stock shot to me.  The owner of the boat would probably love a copy of this.  In another challenge it might have done better, for this particular one, it met the requirement of having yellow in the shot and that''s about it.<br/> <br/>Hope my comments help!<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>Good Luck In Future Challenges!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is a lovely image, the blues, the yellow on the boat, the crisp clear color and image lend itself very well.  The overall balance is also there, very well centered. It meets the challenge in that it has the yellow base for the boat but that''s about all that really jumps out as far as challenge requirements.  The yellow doesn''t dominate the picture nor does it just fade away.  To do better in this paricular challenge you might have desaturated the blue quite a bit to make the yellow stand out more.  But I really like the shot just as it is, a very nice stock shot to me.  The owner of the boat would probably love a copy of this.  In another challenge it might have done better, for this particular one, it met the requirement of having yellow in the shot and that''s about it. Hope my comments help! DeanndaGood Luck In Future Challenges!', '2006-04-16 17:53:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2316441, 315155, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Thought this looked familier, I commented during the challenge!  This is a nice shot, the yellow does stand out but the focus is immediately drawn to the bug and as a result you might have lost a few points for that when people voted.<br/> <br/>A slightly different crop to balance the shot more also might have increased the score just a bit.  Other than that and what I already commented on, I''m sorry I don''t have much else to add. <br/> <br/>Hope my comments have helped and Good Luck in future challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Thought this looked familier, I commented during the challenge!  This is a nice shot, the yellow does stand out but the focus is immediately drawn to the bug and as a result you might have lost a few points for that when people voted. A slightly different crop to balance the shot more also might have increased the score just a bit.  Other than that and what I already commented on, I''m sorry I don''t have much else to add.  Hope my comments have helped and Good Luck in future challenges! Deannda', '2006-04-16 17:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2316448, 315307, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>What can I say?  There is nothing to add that hasn''t already been said, it''s a lovely, beautiful shot, the outtakes were just as beautiful.  Congrats on your ribbon.  I love the shot and have nothing to add.<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. What can I say?  There is nothing to add that hasn''t already been said, it''s a lovely, beautiful shot, the outtakes were just as beautiful.  Congrats on your ribbon.  I love the shot and have nothing to add. DeanndaGood luck in future challenges.', '2006-04-16 17:58:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2316489, 314398, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Wow, what beautiful flowers!  Must be nice to have some to shoot, LOL, where I am it''s still too cold, LOL :)<br/> <br/>This is a lovely idea for yellow and the color is there but it seems a bit flat and dull for the light that seems to be available.  An adjustment on curves or brightness/contrast could really help bring these colors out.  Even a slight adjsutment on the saturation (yellow) would really help this.  <br/> <br/>Also the overall composition seems a bit off to me the balance isn''t quite there, the bud on the right is throwing the whole line off of the flowers, if you bring the crop in just a bit and take out the one bud, leaving a line from bottom to top taking me in and out of the shot.  <br/> <br/>More focus on the full blooms also might help, having a shallow DOF can work with this shot if the focus is on the main bloom.<br/> <br/>I really like the shot overall and the idea behind it, if you do rework this at all I would love to see the results.<br/> <br/>Hope my comments help!<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>Good Luck in future Challenges</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Wow, what beautiful flowers!  Must be nice to have some to shoot, LOL, where I am it''s still too cold, LOL :) This is a lovely idea for yellow and the color is there but it seems a bit flat and dull for the light that seems to be available.  An adjustment on curves or brightness/contrast could really help bring these colors out.  Even a slight adjsutment on the saturation (yellow) would really help this.   Also the overall composition seems a bit off to me the balance isn''t quite there, the bud on the right is throwing the whole line off of the flowers, if you bring the crop in just a bit and take out the one bud, leaving a line from bottom to top taking me in and out of the shot.   More focus on the full blooms also might help, having a shallow DOF can work with this shot if the focus is on the main bloom. I really like the shot overall and the idea behind it, if you do rework this at all I would love to see the results. Hope my comments help! DeanndaGood Luck in future Challenges', '2006-04-16 18:11:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2316535, 315806, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Definitely yellow. But, I have to agree with LucidLotus, it''s hard to get excited about.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Somewhat boring. This is probably what killed it for you. Composition is such that it is a nice shot of a flower, but it doesn''t transend that into being a great shot.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Subject is clear, as it fills the frame, it would be hard to miss the subject.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Color, focus, and light):</b> <br/>Color is nice, feels natural.<br/>Focus may be a bit soft, but perhaps you didn''t apply enough sharpening after resize.<br/>Lighting: Exposure is good, but the lighting in general doesn''t give the image any POP.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I think DPC is going through an anti-flower stage. That might have hurt your vote. Also, voters want to be wowed.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>It''s a pretty picture, don''t get me wrong. It just doesn''t have any wow factor to get high votes.<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: Definitely yellow. But, I have to agree with LucidLotus, it''s hard to get excited about. Composition: Somewhat boring. This is probably what killed it for you. Composition is such that it is a nice shot of a flower, but it doesn''t transend that into being a great shot. Subject: Subject is clear, as it fills the frame, it would be hard to miss the subject. Technical (Color, focus, and light): Color is nice, feels natural.Focus may be a bit soft, but perhaps you didn''t apply enough sharpening after resize.Lighting: Exposure is good, but the lighting in general doesn''t give the image any POP. To grow its vote?: I think DPC is going through an anti-flower stage. That might have hurt your vote. Also, voters want to be wowed. Summary: It''s a pretty picture, don''t get me wrong. It just doesn''t have any wow factor to get high votes. Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-04-16 18:50:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2316541, 315256, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Wow, no comments? How''d that happen? It''s a nice stock flower shot, but doesn''t have anything to draw the voter to the top end of the scale.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I hate to say it, but the composition is boring. Half the frame is flower, half background. It just doesn''t have anything that grabs your eye.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Subject is clear and in focus. DoF works well here.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Color, focus, and light):</b> <br/>Focus looks good. Color may be a bit over-saturated, but looks good. Lighting seems a bit on the harsh side for a flower shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Stay away from the flowers ;-) Really, I think DPC is going through an anti-flower stage, This image should have at least scored in the 5+ range.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Flower shots are pretty, but making one that really slaps a voter in the face and makes them want to give it a high score is hard. Flower shots are like opinions, everyone has one, so they are hard to pass off.<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: Wow, no comments? How''d that happen? It''s a nice stock flower shot, but doesn''t have anything to draw the voter to the top end of the scale. Composition: I hate to say it, but the composition is boring. Half the frame is flower, half background. It just doesn''t have anything that grabs your eye. Subject: Subject is clear and in focus. DoF works well here. Technical (Color, focus, and light): Focus looks good. Color may be a bit over-saturated, but looks good. Lighting seems a bit on the harsh side for a flower shot. To grow its vote?: Stay away from the flowers ;-) Really, I think DPC is going through an anti-flower stage, This image should have at least scored in the 5+ range. Summary: Flower shots are pretty, but making one that really slaps a voter in the face and makes them want to give it a high score is hard. Flower shots are like opinions, everyone has one, so they are hard to pass off. Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-04-16 18:56:17.000000', NULL, 0),
