(2317166, 314025, 33392, '<td valign="top">You probably won''t believe this, but I was sure this was your shot when I saw it during voting.  The floor and lighting are almost identical to your "comfort" entry.<br/> <br/>An excellent photo.  I hope you didn''t take the duckie''s doll away too.</td>', 'You probably won''t believe this, but I was sure this was your shot when I saw it during voting.  The floor and lighting are almost identical to your "comfort" entry. An excellent photo.  I hope you didn''t take the duckie''s doll away too.', '2006-04-17 00:37:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2317210, 313780, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I''m generally not one to be harsh on photos, but this looks horrible. It was destroyed by the plastic wrap filter.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Boring, very boring. Although, I appreciate the complementary colors, the comp itself draws very little attention.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>It''s there, I suppose it''s clear, but that''s about it.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Color, focus, and light):</b> <br/>Color is oversaturated. Focus is hindered by a bad choice in filters and lighting is flat.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Leave the artistic filters alone. Really. Voters here want to see photography, not, "Look what this filter can do."<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I really don''t like to sound mean in critiques, but this just appears to be something yellow you shot and "tried" to make it look better with filters. <br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: I''m generally not one to be harsh on photos, but this looks horrible. It was destroyed by the plastic wrap filter. Composition: Boring, very boring. Although, I appreciate the complementary colors, the comp itself draws very little attention. Subject: It''s there, I suppose it''s clear, but that''s about it. Technical (Color, focus, and light): Color is oversaturated. Focus is hindered by a bad choice in filters and lighting is flat. To grow its vote?: Leave the artistic filters alone. Really. Voters here want to see photography, not, "Look what this filter can do." Summary: I really don''t like to sound mean in critiques, but this just appears to be something yellow you shot and "tried" to make it look better with filters.  Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-04-17 00:53:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2318225, 315438, 30454, '<td valign="top">This is really nice Amy. Cogrates on your highest so far. Keep them coming. Go Team PixelStorm.</td>', 'This is really nice Amy. Cogrates on your highest so far. Keep them coming. Go Team PixelStorm.', '2006-04-17 08:34:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2318403, 315377, 34192, '<td valign="top">This image is nice - perfectly sharp, decent lighting, good composition.  But (don''t you hate that?) for me, the Point of View is awkward.  I am looking down on the child (which lengthens her nose) and I feel I am too close, which leaves me uncomfortable.  An eye level view would be much more flattering to the model and allow me not to feel so, well overbearing as a viewer (that works for some images but I feel it doesn''t work here).  Also, blurring the grass (shorter Depth of Field) would remove some of its texture.  Currently, the texture is distracting as it is not too appealing (brown spots detract).  I can see you have learned to use your camera well.  Now a new learning phase starts in seeing the whole picture before you snap, being able to judge what other will people see. I am currently in that phase too. :)  Good luck!  From what I see in your portfolio, you are moving along quite well.</td>', 'This image is nice - perfectly sharp, decent lighting, good composition.  But (don''t you hate that?) for me, the Point of View is awkward.  I am looking down on the child (which lengthens her nose) and I feel I am too close, which leaves me uncomfortable.  An eye level view would be much more flattering to the model and allow me not to feel so, well overbearing as a viewer (that works for some images but I feel it doesn''t work here).  Also, blurring the grass (shorter Depth of Field) would remove some of its texture.  Currently, the texture is distracting as it is not too appealing (brown spots detract).  I can see you have learned to use your camera well.  Now a new learning phase starts in seeing the whole picture before you snap, being able to judge what other will people see. I am currently in that phase too. :)  Good luck!  From what I see in your portfolio, you are moving along quite well.', '2006-04-17 09:39:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2318505, 312811, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice lines, nice feel, and nice processing.  a little soft, but all the same, it works.  you were probably penalized for the blowouts, but that''s just a dpc thing.  in real life, almost every photo you''ll ever see in a magazine or billboard has blowouts.<br/> <br/>this obviously met the challenge and connected with the viewers--that''s what you need to do.  use this as your bench mark.  when you go out to shoot for a challenge, ask yourself how can you use this awesome tool you have to produce an image that will connect you with more viewers in a positive manner?</td>', 'nice lines, nice feel, and nice processing.  a little soft, but all the same, it works.  you were probably penalized for the blowouts, but that''s just a dpc thing.  in real life, almost every photo you''ll ever see in a magazine or billboard has blowouts. this obviously met the challenge and connected with the viewers--that''s what you need to do.  use this as your bench mark.  when you go out to shoot for a challenge, ask yourself how can you use this awesome tool you have to produce an image that will connect you with more viewers in a positive manner?', '2006-04-17 10:19:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2318571, 314623, 55140, '<td valign="top">Photo''s very clear with good colours. Not the most imaginative entry but quite solid. The colour is more orange than yellow which may have hurt your score a little. I would personaly have cropped a little tighter at the top and possibly made more of the water drops. Good idea and shot though.</td>', 'Photo''s very clear with good colours. Not the most imaginative entry but quite solid. The colour is more orange than yellow which may have hurt your score a little. I would personaly have cropped a little tighter at the top and possibly made more of the water drops. Good idea and shot though.', '2006-04-17 10:40:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2318582, 315744, 31133, '<td valign="top">Nice light!!</td>', 'Nice light!!', '2006-04-17 10:43:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2319076, 312811, 35925, '<td valign="top">Very very nice pic!!!</td>', 'Very very nice pic!!!', '2006-04-17 13:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2320018, 315287, 42100, '<td valign="top">I really liked the colors and tones of this.  I thought the composition and the overall sharpness were very good too.  But I think the main reason I only voted this a six was the shadow/darkness on the left side didn''t look quite natural to me. <br/> <br/>~Mark<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-19 10:32:00.</i></td>', 'I really liked the colors and tones of this.  I thought the composition and the overall sharpness were very good too.  But I think the main reason I only voted this a six was the shadow/darkness on the left side didn''t look quite natural to me.  ~Mark', '2006-04-17 19:16:14.000000', '2006-04-19 11:32:00.000000', 0),
(2320206, 315604, 34192, '<td valign="top">Tilt doesn''t bother me.  Image is good in my opinion.  I think what hurt your score, in this challenge, is people''s desire to have BRIGHT yellow and maybe a more cheery yellow.  Outside the challenge I like this image but I agree with the spot on the face - would rather have it toned down just a little - it doesn''t look quite natural. I like the textures on the wall and the bare bulb.  They definitely add.</td>', 'Tilt doesn''t bother me.  Image is good in my opinion.  I think what hurt your score, in this challenge, is people''s desire to have BRIGHT yellow and maybe a more cheery yellow.  Outside the challenge I like this image but I agree with the spot on the face - would rather have it toned down just a little - it doesn''t look quite natural. I like the textures on the wall and the bare bulb.  They definitely add.', '2006-04-17 20:30:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2320212, 315099, 34192, '<td valign="top">okay, so your car is more dynamic than mine.  Ha!  It is an excellent image and I love the composition/crop you did.  Really generates action in the image.</td>', 'okay, so your car is more dynamic than mine.  Ha!  It is an excellent image and I love the composition/crop you did.  Really generates action in the image.', '2006-04-17 20:33:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2321219, 315226, 23394, '<td valign="top">i''d love to be able to shoot something like this in <i>my living room</i> ;-)<br/> <br/>excellent shot, slippy, and a nice finish in a monster challenge. i have that same lens, but hardly ever use it; i was thinking about selling it, but this shot makes me want to hang onto it.</td>', 'i''d love to be able to shoot something like this in my living room ;-) excellent shot, slippy, and a nice finish in a monster challenge. i have that same lens, but hardly ever use it; i was thinking about selling it, but this shot makes me want to hang onto it.', '2006-04-18 06:34:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2321271, 315665, 23394, '<td valign="top">too subtle for the challenge, but still a cool shot.</td>', 'too subtle for the challenge, but still a cool shot.', '2006-04-18 07:32:49.000000', NULL, 0),
